# AI-Bibliometrics — Docker build context filter.
#
# Docs Reference: docs/08 Security.md §1 (secret handling).
#
# WHY AN ALLOWLIST: the build context is the repo root (`context: .` in
# docker-compose.yml), and Docker ships EVERY file in it to the daemon —
# including gitignored ones. `.gitignore` has no effect on this. An allowlist
# fails closed, so a newly added secret file is excluded by default instead of
# leaking because someone forgot to update a denylist.
#
# PATTERN NOTE: use `**`, never a bare `*`. Docker matches .dockerignore
# patterns against the full path and `*` does NOT cross a `/` separator, so a
# bare `*` would only filter root-level entries and `backend/**` would still
# ship in full.
#
# WHEN YOU ADD A PATH THE IMAGE NEEDS, add an explicit `!` re-allow below.
# A forgotten re-allow fails the build loudly, which is the intended behaviour.

# Deny everything, at any depth.
**

# Re-allow exactly what docker/backend.Dockerfile consumes:
#   - requirements.txt  (pip install -r)
#   - backend/          (COPY backend/ ./backend/)
!requirements.txt
!backend/**

# ...then drop build noise from inside those re-allowed trees.
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
